# interface file - wlan0 added (FIRMWARE.md sec 17/18) for the WiFi
# credentials fetched from the real device. wpa_supplicant itself is started
# by S01wifi (it associates first; ifup's own udhcpc then gets the DHCP
# lease) - Buildroot's wpa_supplicant package doesn't ship the Debian-style
# ifupdown wpa-conf hook, confirmed by checking /etc/network/if-pre-up.d/ has
# no such script.
#
# BOOT-01 (2026-10-05): Buildroot's auto-generated eth0 stanza is gone. The
# KE has no Ethernet (both MACs are disabled in the DT, CONFIG_INGENIC_MAC is
# off), so eth0 never exists and its `wait-delay 15` made S40network's
# `ifup -a` sleep 15 s on every boot (measured: udevd 23.7 s -> memguard
# 40.2 s). Do not add an interface here that the hardware does not have.

auto lo
iface lo inet loopback

auto wlan0
iface wlan0 inet dhcp
  wait-delay 15
